External is fine.
The third section is 'Schema' and there's only a couple things I want to go over here. Never ever trust Auto detect and I saved Attribute 1-3 as Type:Boolean because they are qualitative data points. This seems inaccurate given they were numbers for quite a few iterations and that is usually a quantitative data property, but I have never done any math with them. They were only numbers because not all databases have a Boolean data type and those that do likely have an Int data type that takes up less storage than a Boolean and as weird as this sounds, comparing Integer values is sometimes faster than comparing Booleans. So my choice at this point is 'Do I care more about storage costs and efficiency of processing?' or 'Do I prefer to prevent mathematical operations and more accurately represent the data point?' Integers process fast, Boolean protects the data. GCP is storing this tiny data set for free and database querying is such a massive improvement over spreadsheet nested IFs, this will still process faster with Boolean protections.

